# Worldiversity

## Supabase Setup

All platforms use the same Supabase project by default:

- `SUPABASE_URL`: `https://cdplrbpfgkeqqsrdwagm.supabase.co`
- `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`: configured in `lib/core/config/app_config.dart`

You can override those values at build/run time with:

```bash
flutter run --dart-define=SUPABASE_URL=... --dart-define=SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=...
```

Recommended local commands:

```bash
# iPhone simulator or physical iPhone
RUBYOPT=-rlogger PATH=$HOME/.gem/ruby/2.6.0/bin:$HOME/development/flutter/bin:$PATH \
flutter run -d <device-id> \
  --dart-define=SUPABASE_URL=https://cdplrbpfgkeqqsrdwagm.supabase.co \
  --dart-define=SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_6r6s2GFjs9P9UbsK6euF3Q__l4LzQ15

# Web
flutter build web --release \
  --dart-define=SUPABASE_URL=https://cdplrbpfgkeqqsrdwagm.supabase.co \
  --dart-define=SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_6r6s2GFjs9P9UbsK6euF3Q__l4LzQ15

# Android
flutter build apk --release \
  --dart-define=SUPABASE_URL=https://cdplrbpfgkeqqsrdwagm.supabase.co \
  --dart-define=SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_6r6s2GFjs9P9UbsK6euF3Q__l4LzQ15
```

Firebase/FCM is optional for local compatibility. If platform Firebase files are
missing, the app continues with Supabase features and skips push setup.

Required values:
- `SUPABASE_URL`
- `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`

Utility scripts (`check_db.dart`, `check_storage.dart`, `upload_to_supabase.dart`, `upload_to_supabase_v2.dart`) now read credentials from environment variables:
- `SUPABASE_URL`
- `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` (for read/client scripts)
- `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` (only for admin upload script)

Never commit real service role keys to the repository.

## VS Code Run Config

This repo includes `.vscode/launch.json` with `--dart-define` values.
Update:
- `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_replace_me`

Then run `Flutter (Supabase)` from VS Code Run and Debug.

## Release Builds

Android APK:

```bash
flutter build apk --release --dart-define=SUPABASE_URL=... --dart-define=SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=...
```

Windows (auto copia al Escritorio con secuencia por version):

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\build_release_apk.ps1
```

Opcional:
- `-OutputDir "C:\ruta\carpeta"` para cambiar destino.
- `-AlsoCopyToRepoUpdates` para copiar tambien en `updates/`.

Android App Bundle:

```bash
flutter build appbundle --release --dart-define=SUPABASE_URL=... --dart-define=SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=...
```

## GitHub Auto Deploy (Web + APK)

This repo now includes GitHub Actions:

- `.github/workflows/deploy_web_netlify.yml`
  - On every push to `main`, builds `web` and deploys to Netlify production.
- `.github/workflows/build_android_apk.yml`
  - On every push to `main`, builds release APK and uploads artifact.
  - On tag pushes like `v1.0.39`, also publishes APK files into GitHub Release.

Required GitHub repository secrets:

- `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN`
- `NETLIFY_SITE_ID`

How to get them:

1. Netlify user menu -> `User settings` -> `Applications` -> create `Personal access token` -> use as `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN`.
2. Netlify site -> `Site configuration` -> `General` -> `Site details` -> copy `Site ID` -> use as `NETLIFY_SITE_ID`.

## Supabase Validation Checklist

1. `Authentication > Providers`: enable only providers you use.
2. `Table Editor`: enable RLS on all app tables.
3. `Policies`: enforce ownership checks (for example `auth.uid() = user_id`).
4. `Storage > Policies`: restrict upload/update/delete to owner paths.
5. `Logs`: verify no suspicious API/DB/storage usage after key rotation.

## RLS SQL Starter

There is a starter SQL policy file for this app:
- `supabase/rls_policies.sql`
- `supabase/post_apply_checks.sql` (verification queries)

Apply it from Supabase SQL Editor, then test app flows:
- login/register
- create post/comment/like/save
- chat send/read
- notifications read/update/delete

Recommended order:
1. Run `supabase/rls_policies.sql`
2. Run `supabase/post_apply_checks.sql`
3. Confirm all app tables show `rls_enabled = true`
